content:
Sweep HubSpot for contacts created since the last run whose lifecycle stage is still lead or subscriber and which have no logged outbound engagement. From those, draft for a lead when at least one holds:
- they submitted a form that asked a question or requested contact;
- they hold a role that could buy or champion what you sell;
- their company matches a segment already present in closed-won deals;
- they returned to the site or opened more than one asset.

Skip, and log why: personal email domains with no company, competitors, students and job seekers, obvious spam submissions, anyone already in an open deal, and anyone a colleague has emailed in the last five days — two people touching the same lead in a week is worse than nobody.

Order the batch by how much response budget is left, most urgent first, so an overdue lead is the first thing seen in the channel. When more than ten leads qualify in one sweep, draft the ten most urgent and say plainly how many were left for the next pass.
